  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Literal sample-cell text.\n\nAdded: WithExampleText declares the exact text a generated sample cell should carry, exposed as\nIImportColumn.ExampleText. WithExample is typed to the destination property, so a column converted from text into a\ncollection could not carry a usable example: the value was rendered through Convert.ToString as its type name, and\nmarking such a column NotEmpty made the generated template fail its own parse on the blank cell. ExampleText wins\nover WithExample and over the value read from a supplied example model.\n\nNote: IImportColumn gained a member. It is a read-only metadata view produced by ImportRule<T>.Columns and is\nnot an extension point, so this affects only code that implements the interface itself.\n\nPrevious release notes follow.\n\n6.0.0 — Template generation and reader hardening.\n\nAdded: ImportRule<T>.Columns exposes ordered column metadata via the new public IImportColumn; new declarative\nrule methods Describe, WithExample, WithExpectedFormat, WithEnumSource, WithAllowedValues, WithAliases;\nImportRule<T>.BuildTemplate generates a two-sheet xlsx (fillable data sheet first, legend second) with styled and\nfrozen headers, sample rows, localizable legend captions and in-cell dropdowns sourced from the legend;\nReadXlsx(stream, sheetName) selects a worksheet by name; TryReadXlsx/TryReadCsv aggregate every cell error instead\nof throwing on the first; new MissingColumnsException, DuplicateColumnException and SheetNotFoundException;\nInvalidCellValueException now carries a structured ImportError.\n\nFixed: header cells are read positionally, so a blank or leading-blank header cell no longer shifts every column\nsilently; cells are stringified culture-invariantly, so decimals and dates no longer break under a non-invariant\nserver culture; required columns are validated up front instead of surfacing as a misleading row-2 cell error;\nfully blank rows are skipped; enum conversion rejects undefined numeric values; duplicate headers and unsettable\nproperties throw typed ImportExceptions instead of raw ArgumentException/InvalidOperationException; constant and\ncomputed columns no longer require a header to be present; header matching collapses inner whitespace runs.\n\nBreaking: IPropertyRule (internal) is replaced by the public IImportColumn; the internal ReadFromType enum is\nreplaced by the public ImportValueSource; WriteValue and ReadFromModel now return the rule for chaining;\nRuleFor throws immediately when the property does not exist on the model; an optional mapped column may now be\nabsent from the file instead of failing every row.",
